{
  "paper_id": "nar2026-gkag709",
  "title": "CNEwrap: a scalable toolkit with a novel algorithm for large-scale genome-wide accelerated conserved non-coding elements detection.",
  "doi": "10.1093/nar/gkag709",
  "journal": "Nucleic Acids Research",
  "data_url": "https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.29625779",
  "verified": {
    "opened_data_files": true,
    "what_i_actually_checked": "Downloaded and unpacked SimData.zip (7.68 MB) and ScienceData.zip (10.25 MB) from FigShare article 29625779 v5 (CC BY 4.0, no login). Counted: 3 simulation sets (ratites 16 species, reptiles 14 species, reptiles2 14 species), each one 500-row BED plus four FASTA files (CaseA/B/C = 1/2/3 accelerated clades, CaseZ = null), 200 bp per locus, so 6,000 labelled locus-alignments. Real set: hg38_science_rename.bed has 10,032 rows and 10,032 unique hCONDEL IDs; hg38_science_verified.csv has 803 IDs; 1,701 per-element FASTA alignments each with exactly 10 mammal sequences (confirmed in phyloacc-aln-stats.csv, 1,701 rows, num-seqs = 10 for all; alignment length median 142 bp, min 4, max 3,320). I computed the key overlap myself: 127 of the 803 experimentally validated hCONDELs have an alignment here, and the second set has 4,669 unique HAR/human-gained-enhancer IDs, 532 validated, 352 scored, 12 overlapping. Read Simulation_ACC.R to learn that BED columns 6 and 7 are the per-locus simulated conserved and accelerated substitution rates, and run_cnewrap.sh to confirm PO = accelerated loci and NE = CaseZ null loci. Then reproduced the paper's own benchmark using the exact score columns its plotting script uses (ave_score for EvoAcc, lnlratio for phyloP, logbf1 for PhyloAcc, weightedPearsonCorrelationCoeff for ForwardGenomics): PhyloAcc reaches AUROC 0.997-1.000 in all six case-by-taxon combinations, phyloP 0.568-1.000, while EvoAcc's ave_score gives 0.371/0.194/0.003 (reptile A/B/C) and 0.693/0.665/0.016 (ratite A/B/C), and no single sign flip fixes it. A single trivial feature, the raw count of variable sites in the alignment, reaches AUROC 0.827-0.997 across all six.",
    "what_came_from_paper_text_only": "The claim that EvoAcc outperforms PhyloAcc, phyloP and ForwardGenomics on simulated data, and the published real-data counts (EvoAcc 34, PhyloAcc 4, phyloP 6, ForwardGenomics 0 of the 127 validated hCONDELs; 5/4/6/0 of the 12 validated enhancers). I did not open CNEWRAP.zip (111.8 MB) or scripts_for_figures.7z (52.8 MB), both over the 50 MB cap, so I could not check whether those archives contain figure-source tables that differ from the results_collection archives I did open. The provenance of the MPRA (massively parallel reporter assay) labels is from the paper plus a search: they are taken from Xue et al., Science 2023, using that study's own significance thresholds."
  },
  "part_a_killers": {
    "a1_downloadable": {"pass": true, "note": "Verified by downloading: FigShare 29625779 v5, CC BY 4.0, 18 files, no login or application. The two files I needed (SimData.zip, ScienceData.zip) are 7.7 and 10.2 MB."},
    "a2_label_is_a_column": {"pass": true, "note": "No inference needed, but the label is not literally a column. For simulated loci it is the identity of the FASTA file (CaseA/B/C accelerated vs CaseZ null) plus per-locus true rates in BED columns 6-7; for real elements it is membership in an 803-ID list joined on hCONDEL ID. Both are clean assignments I performed successfully."},
    "a3_inputs_present": {"pass": true, "note": "Verified: actual aligned nucleotide sequences are in the files, not accession numbers. Simulated FASTAs hold 14-16 species concatenated across 500 loci; each real element is a 10-species alignment."},
    "a4_units_stated": {"pass": true, "note": "Sequence data needs no units and alignment lengths are in base pairs. The two continuous label columns (simulated conserved and accelerated substitution rates) carry no header and no stated units; I recovered their meaning only by reading Simulation_ACC.R."},
    "a5_enough_rows": {"pass": true, "n_rows": 6000, "note": "Verified by counting: 500 loci x 4 scenarios x 3 simulation sets = 6,000 labelled 200 bp alignments, half of them negatives. Real external set is 1,701 elements with 127 positives."},
    "a6_fits_laptop": {"pass": true, "working_set": "~0.1 GB", "note": "Verified: 18 MB of zips expand to 11 MB (sim) and 81 MB (real). A 200 bp by 14-row alignment model needs no GPU."},
    "a7_counts_match_paper": {"pass": true, "note": "Unusually good: every number I counted matches the text exactly - 10,032 hCONDELs, 803 validated, 1,701 mapped, 127 validated-and-mapped, 352 enhancers mapped, 12 validated, 500 simulated loci of 200 bp."},
    "a8_label_provenance": {"pass": true, "note": "Simulated labels are the generating parameters of the authors' own simulation, not a model's prediction. Real labels are MPRA (massively parallel reporter assay) measurements from Xue et al., Science 2023. Caveat: the released EvoAcc, phyloP, PhyloAcc and ForwardGenomics per-locus scores are model outputs and may only be used as baselines, never as features."
  },
